Here is a function to find the highest common ancestor of two nodes in a binary tree:

function findHCA(root, node1, node2)
{
   if (root == null || root == node1 || root == node2)
   {
       return null;
   }
   let node1Parent = find(root, node1)[0];
   let node2Parent = find(root, node2)[0];
   while (node1Parent && node1Parent != null && node2Parent && node2Parent != null)
   {
       if (node1Parent.left == node1 && node2Parent.right == node2)
       {
           return node1Parent;
       }
       if (node1Parent.right == node1 && node2Parent.left == node2)
       {
           return node1Parent;
       }
       node1Parent = find(root, node1Parent)[0];
       node2Parent = find(root, node2Parent)[0];
   }
   return null;
}

This function uses the property that the parent of a node is the only ancestor of its children. It first finds the ancestors of the first node using the find function, then it finds the ancestors of the second node using the find function again, and it checks if any of these ancestors are also ancestors of the first node. If the ancestor is found, it is the highest common ancestor of the two nodes. If the ancestor is not found, the highest common ancestor of the two nodes is null.
